Marcy's annual pension is $50,000/year. After 20 years, she becomes entitled to 5% of the value of the pension per year. This means that her annual pension will increase by 5% of $50,000, which is $2,500. Therefore, her annual pension will be $50,000 + $2,500 = $52,500/year.

If she quits after 30 years, her annual pension will be $52,500/year.

Final answer: \boxed{52500}
